## On Master:
kubectl get nodes

Expected:
NAME          STATUS   ROLES           AGE
kube-master   Ready    control-plane   20m
kube-worker1  Ready    <none>          5m
kube-worker2  Ready    <none>          3m

Now:
- Master manages the cluster.
- Worker nodes run applications.
- kubelet runs on every node.
- containerd runs containers.
- CNI provides Pod networking.

Congratulations! We have successfully created a multi-node Kubernetes cluster using Kubeadm.

## VERIFY THE CLUSTER INTERNALLY
Now inspect the cluster.
1. Check nodes
kubectl get nodes -o wide

2. Check namespaces
kubectl get namespaces

3. Check system Pods
kubectl get pods -n kube-system

4. Check all Pods
kubectl get pods -A

5. Check cluster information
kubectl cluster-info

6. Check component details
kubectl describe node kube-master

7. Check services
kubectl get services -A

8. Check kubelet
On each node:
sudo systemctl status kubelet

9. Check containerd
sudo systemctl status containerd

10. Check container information
sudo crictl info
